		"name": "Notejam SCIM API - Complete Collection",
		"description": "Complete collection of the Notejam SCIM API with all tested and validated functionalities.\n\n## Included Features:\n\n- All HTTP methods (GET, POST, PUT, PATCH, DELETE)\n- SCIM filters (boolean, numeric, string, date, complex)\n- SCIM pagination\n- Real usage examples based on actual test data\n\n## IMPORTANT:\n\nThe `customFields` field must be sent as a JSON string: `\"customFields\": \"{\\\"test\\\": \\\"value\\\"}\"`\n\n## Step-by-Step Testing Instructions:\n\n### 1. Setup:\n\n- Import this collection into Postman\n- Configure the `baseUrl` variable in the collection variables\n- Ensure the Notejam application is running on the configured URL\n\n### 2. Basic CRUD Testing:\n\n1. Start with \"COMPLETE DEMO\" folder\n2. Run \"Automatic Demo - PADS\" to verify basic connectivity\n3. Run \"Automatic Demo - NOTES\" to verify notes endpoint\n4. Execute \"Individual Filter Test\" requests to validate SCIM filtering\n\n### 3. Full CRUD Operations:\n\n1. **PADS - Complete CRUD** folder:\n   - GET /pads (list all pads)\n   - POST /pads (create new pad)\n   - GET /pads/{id} (retrieve specific pad)\n   - PUT /pads/{id} (update pad completely)\n   - PATCH /pads/{id} (partial update)\n   - DELETE /pads/{id} (logical deletion)\n2. **NOTES - Complete CRUD** folder:\n   - Follow the same pattern as PADS\n   - Test all CRUD operations for notes\n\n### 4. SCIM Filter Testing:\n\n1. **SCIM FILTERS - PADS** folder:\n   - Test boolean filters (active eq true/false)\n   - Test numeric filters (status eq 1/2)\n   - Test string filters (name eq \"Test Pad\")\n   - Test date filters (created gt \"2025-08-28T00:00:00\", modified gt \"2025-08-28T20:00:00\")\n   - Test complex filters (active eq true and status eq 1)\n2. **SCIM FILTERS - NOTES** folder:\n   - Test similar filter patterns for notes\n   - Test date filters for notes creation and modification\n   - Verify text-based filtering works correctly\n\n### 5. Pagination Testing:\n\n1. **SCIM PAGINATION** folder:\n   - Test first page (startIndex=1, count=5)\n   - Test second page (startIndex=6, count=5)\n   - Verify totalResults count is accurate\n\n### 6. Advanced Examples:\n\n1. **ADVANCED SAMPLES** folder:\n   - Test filter + pagination combinations\n   - Verify complex queries work correctly\n\n### 7. Validation:\n\n- All requests should return appropriate HTTP status codes\n- GET requests should return 200 OK\n- POST requests should return 201 Created\n- PUT/PATCH requests should return 204 No Content\n- DELETE requests should return 204 No Content\n- Check that response bodies contain expected data structure\n- Verify that filters return the correct number of results\n- Ensure pagination works correctly with totalResults\n\n### 8. Troubleshooting:\n\n- If requests fail, check the application logs\n- Verify the `baseUrl` variable is correctly set\n- Ensure the database is accessible and contains test data\n- Check that all required services are running\n\n### 9. Expected Results:\n\n- All CRUD operations should work without errors\n- SCIM filters should return filtered results\n- Pagination should work with proper totalResults\n- JSON Patch operations should update specific fields only\n- Soft delete should mark records as inactive but not remove them\n\n## Notes:\n\n- This collection uses real IDs from the test database\n- All requests include proper Content-Type headers\n- Test scripts validate response structure automatically\n- The collection is ready for demonstration and production use",
		"schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
		"_exporter_id": "47263824",
